# T19b: "A payload holds values only: numbers, Bool, Char, text and arrays held by value (its own copy), error values,
# and enums and structs of those". A field of text is accepted, but text one level down is refused as "holds a
# reference": a struct holding a String, an enum case holding one, an Array<String>, and an error value whose own
# payload holds text (PErr.Bad(msg String) inside WErr.Wrap) - each "payload field ... holds a reference - a payload
# holds values only". With the inner payload a number (scratch/nest2.olang) the error value field works, built and
# interpreted alike.
import "std/io"
type Loc struct(file String, line I64) { file, line }
type Sh enum { Named(t String), Anon }
type PErr error { Bad(msg String), Eof }
type QErr error { At(at Loc), Kind(s Sh), Arr(a Array<String>), Wrap(inner PErr) }
fn main() {
    x QErr = QErr.At(Loc("f", 3))
    io.Println($x)!
}
